<p>Colors on the display are produced using the three colors of RGB, but 
 colors in print are composed of the four colors of CMYK. For printing, 
 RGB color must be converted to CMYK color.</p>
<p>When converting the color, you can adjust the color tones by changing 
 the color profiling pattern.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only for color printers.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Settings</span> 
 for <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 button to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Details</span> dialog box and 
 click the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile:</span> 
 list, select a <a class="help-popup-link" data-help-popup="true" href="~/Topics/IDH_CCOLORPROFILE">color profile pattern</a>.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">User Setting</span>, 
 click the <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> button to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile Details</span> dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Make detailed color profile settings for each 
 element of your document (<span class="Term-Soft">Text:</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Graphic:</span>, 
 and <span class="Term-Soft">Photo:</span>).</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Adding a Color Profile</h2>
<p>You can add the new color profile provided by the developer to the list 
 and use it.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile 
 Settings...</span> button to open the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span> box, 
 enter a name.<br/>
 If you want to edit an existing color profile, select the color profile 
 pattern in the <span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>In <span class="Term-Soft">Path/File Name:</span> 
 or <span class="Term-Soft">Browse...</span>, specify the path name and file 
 name of the color profile data to be used.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Add</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span> to save.<br/>
 If you click <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span>, the dialog box to 
 confirm whether or not to save the change appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile:</span> 
 list, select the color profile pattern you added to the list.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
